---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Publishing and site policy"
  description="How this site labels scenarios, handles reader data, accepts corrections, and states content-use preferences."
>
  <h1>Publishing and site policy</h1>

  <h2>Author and scenario labels</h2>
  <p>
    I write this site in a personal capacity. The views are mine. They do not represent a current
    or former employer. A post that uses a composite or illustrative scenario says so before the
    scenario starts.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p>
    Each post links to a public correction form. A correction should identify the article, the
    smallest affected section, and a primary source when one is available. I update the visible
    date when a factual or technical change alters the article.
  </p>

  <h2>Content use</h2>
  <p>
    Ahmed Sheta owns the written content unless a page states another owner or license. Search
    indexing and references to the public pages are permitted. The site's machine-readable
    content signal does not grant permission to use the content for AI training.
  </p>
  <p>
    The repository source does not carry an open-source license. Public access to the repository
    does not grant permission to reuse its code or content.
  </p>
  <p>
    Code examples explain a technical idea. They omit environment-specific controls and do not
    include a warranty. Test an example against the current service documentation before you use
    it in a production system.
  </p>

  <h2>Reader data</h2>
  <p>
    The site does not run advertising or audience analytics. It does not set a site cookie. The
    theme and reading-voice controls store their settings in the reader's browser. Cloudflare
    serves the site and processes the request data needed to deliver and protect it.
  </p>
  <p>
    Topic and correction links open GitHub. GitHub applies its own account and privacy policies.
  </p>
</Base>
